<hr data-start=3D"392" data-end=3D"395">
<h2 data-start=3D"397" data-end=3D"415">1. Introduction</h2>
<p data-start=3D"417" data-end=3D"621">En CSS, <strong data-start=3D"425" d=
ata-end=3D"474">tout =C3=A9l=C3=A9ment HTML est une bo=C3=AEte rectangulair=
e</strong> =E2=80=94 c=E2=80=99est ce qu=E2=80=99on appelle le <strong data=
-start=3D"503" data-end=3D"522">mod=C3=A8le de bo=C3=AEte</strong> (box mod=
el). Comprendre ce mod=C3=A8le est fondamental pour ma=C3=AEtriser la mise =
en page et le design web.</p>
<p data-start=3D"623" data-end=3D"719">Chaque bo=C3=AEte est compos=C3=A9e =
de plusieurs couches, qui s=E2=80=99empilent de l=E2=80=99int=C3=A9rieur ve=
rs l=E2=80=99ext=C3=A9rieur :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"721" data-end=3D"892">
<li data-start=3D"721" data-end=3D"755">
<p data-start=3D"723" data-end=3D"755"><strong data-start=3D"723" data-end=
=3D"734">Contenu</strong> (texte, image, etc.)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"756" data-end=3D"807">
<p data-start=3D"758" data-end=3D"807"><strong data-start=3D"758" data-end=
=3D"769">Padding</strong> (espace int=C3=A9rieur, autour du contenu)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"808" data-end=3D"830">
<p data-start=3D"810" data-end=3D"830"><strong data-start=3D"810" data-end=
=3D"820">Border</strong> (bordure)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"831" data-end=3D"892">
<p data-start=3D"833" data-end=3D"892"><strong data-start=3D"833" data-end=
=3D"843">Margin</strong> (espace ext=C3=A9rieur, s=C3=A9parant la bo=C3=AEt=
e des autres)</p>
</li>
</ul>
