<h3 data-start=3D"5607" data-end=3D"5659">7.6 Collapsing margin (marges qui=
 se fusionnent)</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"5661" data-end=3D"5906">
<li data-start=3D"5661" data-end=3D"5763">
<p data-start=3D"5663" data-end=3D"5763">Les marges verticales entre deux =
=C3=A9l=C3=A9ments cons=C3=A9cutifs peuvent fusionner pour ne former qu=E2=
=80=99une marge.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5764" data-end=3D"5906">
<p data-start=3D"5766" data-end=3D"5906">Exemple : un <code data-start=3D"5=
779" data-end=3D"5794">margin-bottom</code> de 20px suivi d=E2=80=99un <cod=
e data-start=3D"5814" data-end=3D"5826">margin-top</code> de 30px entre deu=
x =C3=A9l=C3=A9ments ne fera pas 50px, mais 30px (la plus grande marge).</p=
>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"5908" data-end=3D"5911">
<h2 data-start=3D"5913" data-end=3D"5941">8. Le mod=C3=A8le <code data-star=
t=3D"5929" data-end=3D"5941">box-sizing</code></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"5943" data-end=3D"5963">8.1 Introduction</h3>
<p data-start=3D"5965" data-end=3D"6111">Par d=C3=A9faut, <code data-start=
=3D"5977" data-end=3D"5984">width</code> et <code data-start=3D"5988" data-=
end=3D"5996">height</code> ne prennent en compte que la taille du contenu (=
<code data-start=3D"6045" data-end=3D"6058">content-box</code>), donc <code=
 data-start=3D"6066" data-end=3D"6075">padding</code> et <code data-start=
=3D"6079" data-end=3D"6087">border</code> s=E2=80=99ajoutent <strong data-s=
tart=3D"6099" data-end=3D"6110">en plus</strong>.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"6113" data-end=3D"6144">8.2 Changer ce comportement</h3>
<pre class=3D"overflow-visible!" data-start=3D"6146" data-end=3D"6195"><div=
