<h3 data-start=3D"1794" data-end=3D"1832">2.3. Images et m=C3=A9dias adapta=
tifs</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1833" data-end=3D"1989">Les images doivent =C3=AAtre redim=
ensionn=C3=A9es automatiquement, et parfois remplac=C3=A9es par des version=
s plus l=C3=A9g=C3=A8res selon la r=C3=A9solution (technique du <code data-=
start=3D"1976" data-end=3D"1987">&lt;picture&gt;</code>).</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1991" data-end=3D"2017">2.4. Flexbox et Grid</h3>
<p data-start=3D"2018" data-end=3D"2124">Ce sont des syst=C3=A8mes de mise =
en page modernes permettant une organisation flexible et fluide des =C3=A9l=
=C3=A9ments.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2126" data-end=3D"2129">
<h2 data-start=3D"2131" data-end=3D"2192">3. Pourquoi penser aussi =C3=A0 l=
=E2=80=99accessibilit=C3=A9 en Responsive ?</h2>
<p data-start=3D"2194" data-end=3D"2452">L=E2=80=99accessibilit=C3=A9 web v=
ise =C3=A0 rendre un site utilisable par <strong data-start=3D"2251" data-e=
nd=3D"2268">tout le monde</strong>, y compris les personnes avec des handic=
aps visuels, moteurs, cognitifs ou auditifs. Le responsive design doit donc=
 int=C3=A9grer des bonnes pratiques pour ne pas exclure ces utilisateurs.</=
p>
<hr data-start=3D"2454" data-end=3D"2457">
<h2 data-start=3D"2459" data-end=3D"2517">4. Les enjeux de l=E2=80=99access=
ibilit=C3=A9 en contexte responsive</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"2519" data-end=3D"2559">4.1. Taille et lisibilit=C3=A9 du=
 texte</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2560" data-end=3D"2759">
<li data-start=3D"2560" data-end=3D"2619">
<p data-start=3D"2562" data-end=3D"2619">Utiliser des tailles de police fle=
xibles (<code data-start=3D"2604" data-end=3D"2609">rem</code>, <code data-=
start=3D"2611" data-end=3D"2615">em</code>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2620" data-end=3D"2673">
<p data-start=3D"2622" data-end=3D"2673">Pr=C3=A9voir un bon contraste coul=
eur (fond vs texte).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2674" data-end=3D"2759">
<p data-start=3D"2676" data-end=3D"2759">Permettre le zoom sans casser la m=
ise en page (=C3=A9viter les tailles fixes en pixels).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"2761" data-end=3D"2802">4.2. Navigation claire et coh=C3=
=A9rente</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2803" data-end=3D"3010">
<li data-start=3D"2803" data-end=3D"2865">
<p data-start=3D"2805" data-end=3D"2865">Des menus accessibles au clavier (=
tabulation, raccourcis).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2866" data-end=3D"2950">
<p data-start=3D"2868" data-end=3D"2950">Des boutons assez grands pour =C3=
=AAtre touch=C3=A9s facilement sur mobile (min. 44x44px).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2951" data-end=3D"3010">
<p data-start=3D"2953" data-end=3D"3010">=C3=89viter les zones cliquables t=
rop petites ou trop proches.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"3012" data-end=3D"3042">4.3. Contenus adaptables</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3043" data-end=3D"3240">
<li data-start=3D"3043" data-end=3D"3132">
<p data-start=3D"3045" data-end=3D"3132">Ne pas cacher des informations ess=
entielles dans des menus mobiles sans alternatives.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3133" data-end=3D"3240">
<p data-start=3D"3135" data-end=3D"3240">Fournir des alternatives textuelle=
s pour les images (<code data-start=3D"3188" data-end=3D"3193">alt</code>),=
 vid=C3=A9os (sous-titres), sons (transcriptions).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"3242" data-end=3D"3270">4.4. Gestion des focus</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3271" data-end=3D"3380">
<li data-start=3D"3271" data-end=3D"3340">
<p data-start=3D"3273" data-end=3D"3340">Styles visibles sur les =C3=A9l=C3=
=A9ments en focus clavier (<code data-start=3D"3324" data-end=3D"3332">:foc=
us</code> CSS).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3341" data-end=3D"3380">
<p data-start=3D"3343" data-end=3D"3380">Eviter de supprimer le focus visib=
le.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3382" data-end=3D"3385">
<h2 data-start=3D"3387" data-end=3D"3464">5. Comment impl=C3=A9menter le re=
sponsive design avec l=E2=80=99accessibilit=C3=A9 en t=C3=AAte ?</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"3466" data-end=3D"3508">5.1. Mobile-first + accessible-fi=
rst</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3509" data-end=3D"3634">
<li data-start=3D"3509" data-end=3D"3556">
<p data-start=3D"3511" data-end=3D"3556">Concevoir d=E2=80=99abord pour le =
plus petit =C3=A9cran.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3557" data-end=3D"3634">
<p data-start=3D"3559" data-end=3D"3634">Tester la navigation au clavier et=
 avec des lecteurs d=E2=80=99=C3=A9cran d=C3=A8s le d=C3=A9part.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"3636" data-end=3D"3672">5.2. Structure HTML s=C3=A9mantiq=
ue</h3>
<p data-start=3D"3673" data-end=3D"3838">Utiliser des balises HTML5 s=C3=A9=
mantiques : <code data-start=3D"3714" data-end=3D"3724">&lt;header&gt;</cod=
e>, <code data-start=3D"3726" data-end=3D"3733">&lt;nav&gt;</code>, <code d=
ata-start=3D"3735" data-end=3D"3743">&lt;main&gt;</code>, <code data-start=
=3D"3745" data-end=3D"3755">&lt;footer&gt;</code>, <code data-start=3D"3757=
" data-end=3D"3768">&lt;article&gt;</code>, <code data-start=3D"3770" data-=
end=3D"3781">&lt;section&gt;</code> permet aux aides techniques de mieux co=
mprendre la page.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"3840" data-end=3D"3885">5.3. Media queries et contenu dyn=
amique</h3>
<p data-start=3D"3886" data-end=3D"4027">Penser =C3=A0 ce que les contenus =
soient <strong data-start=3D"3922" data-end=3D"3964">accessibles m=C3=AAme =
quand ils sont cach=C3=A9s</strong> par CSS (ex : menu hamburger doit =C3=
=AAtre accessible au clavier).</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"4029" data-end=3D"4083">5.4. Tests r=C3=A9guliers avec ou=
tils d=E2=80=99accessibilit=C3=A9</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"4084" data-end=3D"4275">
<li data-start=3D"4084" data-end=3D"4147">
<p data-start=3D"4086" data-end=3D"4147"><a data-start=3D"4086" data-end=3D=
"4118" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_new" class=3D"cursor-pointer">WAVE</a> :=
 analyse d=E2=80=99accessibilit=C3=A9.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4148" data-end=3D"4187">
<p data-start=3D"4150" data-end=3D"4187">Lecteurs d=E2=80=99=C3=A9cran (NVD=
A, VoiceOver).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4188" data-end=3D"4217">
<p data-start=3D"4190" data-end=3D"4217">Simulation de daltonisme.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4218" data-end=3D"4275">
<p data-start=3D"4220" data-end=3D"4275">Validation WCAG (Web Content Acces=
sibility Guidelines).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4277" data-end=3D"4280">
<h2 data-start=3D"4282" data-end=3D"4305">6. Exemples concrets</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"4307" data-end=3D"4339">6.1. Texte fluide et lisible</h3>
