<h3 data-start=3D"2469" data-end=3D"2494">2.4. Avantages de BEM</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2496" data-end=3D"2671">
<li data-start=3D"2496" data-end=3D"2536">
<p data-start=3D"2498" data-end=3D"2536">Structure claire, facile =C3=A0 co=
mprendre.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2537" data-end=3D"2566">
<p data-start=3D"2539" data-end=3D"2566">=C3=89vite les conflits de noms.</=
p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2567" data-end=3D"2595">
<p data-start=3D"2569" data-end=3D"2595">Facilite la r=C3=A9utilisation.</p=
>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2596" data-end=3D"2623">
<p data-start=3D"2598" data-end=3D"2623">Ind=C3=A9pendance entre blocs.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2624" data-end=3D"2671">
<p data-start=3D"2626" data-end=3D"2671">Tr=C3=A8s utilis=C3=A9 dans les pr=
ojets professionnels.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"2673" data-end=3D"2695">2.5. Inconv=C3=A9nients</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2697" data-end=3D"2808">
<li data-start=3D"2697" data-end=3D"2718">
<p data-start=3D"2699" data-end=3D"2718">Noms parfois longs.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2719" data-end=3D"2757">
<p data-start=3D"2721" data-end=3D"2757">N=C3=A9cessite une discipline rigo=
ureuse.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2758" data-end=3D"2808">
<p data-start=3D"2760" data-end=3D"2808">Peut =C3=AAtre verbeux sur de tr=
=C3=A8s petits composants.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"2810" data-end=3D"2813">
<h2 data-start=3D"2815" data-end=3D"2848">3. OOCSS : Object Oriented CSS</h=
2>
<h3 data-start=3D"2850" data-end=3D"2871">3.1. Pr=C3=A9sentation</h3>
<p data-start=3D"2873" data-end=3D"2982">OOCSS, ou CSS orient=C3=A9 objet, =
a =C3=A9t=C3=A9 popularis=C3=A9 par Nicole Sullivan.<br data-start=3D"2939"=
 data-end=3D"2942">
Il s=E2=80=99appuie sur deux principes majeurs :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2984" data-end=3D"3079">
<li data-start=3D"2984" data-end=3D"3033">
<p data-start=3D"2986" data-end=3D"3033">S=C3=A9parer la <strong data-start=
=3D"2997" data-end=3D"3010">structure</strong> et la <strong data-start=3D"=
3017" data-end=3D"3025">peau</strong> (skin).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3034" data-end=3D"3079">
<p data-start=3D"3036" data-end=3D"3079">S=C3=A9parer la <strong data-start=
=3D"3047" data-end=3D"3060">structure</strong> et le <strong data-start=3D"=
3067" data-end=3D"3078">contenu</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"3081" data-end=3D"3103">3.2. Concepts cl=C3=A9s</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3105" data-end=3D"3365">
<li data-start=3D"3105" data-end=3D"3197">
<p data-start=3D"3107" data-end=3D"3197"><strong data-start=3D"3107" data-e=
nd=3D"3120">Structure</strong> : d=C3=A9finit la forme, la mise en page (ex=
 : largeurs, marges, positionnement).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3198" data-end=3D"3271">
<p data-start=3D"3200" data-end=3D"3271"><strong data-start=3D"3200" data-e=
nd=3D"3215">Peau (skin)</strong> : concerne le style visuel (couleurs, poli=
ces, ombres).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3272" data-end=3D"3365">
<p data-start=3D"3274" data-end=3D"3365"><strong data-start=3D"3274" data-e=
nd=3D"3285">Contenu</strong> : l=E2=80=99information =C3=A0 l=E2=80=99int=
=C3=A9rieur, que le style ne doit pas influencer directement.</p>
</li>
</ul>
